-  "body": "This is for reading a paper in order to judge it. The tools here point you at passages, and\nReferee never returns a verdict. Most of what the modes show links back to the article’s own words, so you can\ncheck it in one click — see [Is the AI reading the article for\nme?](/help/questions#faq-is-the-ai-reading-for-me).\n\nSeveral of these modes are [experimental features](/help/experimental-features): Referee and FAQ\nappear only once you turn those on.\n\n## Before you add it\n\n**Do not put a manuscript you received in confidence through Referee.** It is built for public\npreprints, open-review submissions, and drafts the author has agreed to share.\n[Referee](/help/mode-referee) says why.\n\n## See what the paper claims\n\n- **Open [Referee](/help/mode-referee)** and choose **Claims**: what the paper promises, each\n  beside the passages meant to deliver it. Fewer passages under a claim does not make it a weaker\n  claim.\n- **Open [Ideas](/help/mode-ideas)** for what the piece assumes and never states. That split is the\n  AI’s reading, so treat it as a careful reader’s interpretation.\n- **Try [FAQ](/help/mode-faq)** to find the objections the piece anticipates. Each question points\n  to passages; no answer is written.\n\n## Test it against your criteria\n\n- **Write a criterion** under **Criteria** in Referee, or start from a preset, and press **Run this\n  criterion**. “The model did not find a passage” tells you about the search, not the paper.\n- **Ask [Search](/help/mode-search) by meaning**, for example “where does he concede a weakness?”.\n  The marks [down the spine](/help/spine) show whether the matches sit in one place or run through\n  the whole piece.\n- **Check what it is built on** in [Sources](/help/mode-sources)’ **Bibliography**.\n  **first cited** jumps to where the article first cites a work.\n- **See what others have said** in Sources’ **Reception**, which searches the web. Many pieces\n  turn out to have no reception at all, and it says so. **Claims** lists the claims the paper rests\n  on, for you to check against the web.\n\n## Write your comments\n\n- **Select the words** you are commenting on and write a note — see [Comments and\n  bookmarks](/help/comments). In Referee a box opens first, and nothing is saved until you press\n  **Save** or close it.\n- **Read them back** with **Mirror** in Referee, which flags any comment an author would find hard\n  to act on.\n- **Sort them** in Referee’s **Notes** into major and minor, then copy them out as the bones of\n  your report — your words only, with the passage each one is on.\n- **Carry lines out in the paper’s own words** with [Quotes](/help/mode-quotes).\n\nHow to tell the author’s words from the AI’s is in [The AI’s words and the\nauthor’s](/help/ai-words). If the paper is in your own area, [Reading in your own\nfield](/help/for-experts) covers getting to what is new."
